# Environments and secrets
myenv/
.venv/
.env

# Never commit data or results: both are reproduced from scripts and manifests.
# Anchored to the repository root. Unanchored, `data/` would also match the source
# package src/mflow/data/ and quietly keep the adapters out of every commit.
/data/
/results/

# Source documents. The specification and dataset notes are inputs, not artefacts, and
# are not ours to redistribute. The response to the reviewers is the opposite: it is a
# deliverable generated by make_answer.py, so it is versioned alongside the manuscript.
*.docx
!paper/*/answer.docx

# Python
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*.egg-info/
build/
dist/
.mypy_cache/
.ruff_cache/
.pytest_cache/
.coverage
htmlcov/

# Editors and OS
.DS_Store
.idea/
*.swp

# The toy fixture is deliberately committed: it is the reference implementation of the
# data contract and the M1 acceptance tests depend on it.
!tests/fixtures/toy_site/
.mplcache/

# Scratch directories created by dataset-format probes.
.robod_probe/

# Report artefacts are derived: `mflow report` rebuilds them from results/, and results/
# is itself rebuilt from the run manifests. Committing a table would put a number in the
# repository whose provenance is a file that is not here.
# The contents rather than the directory itself, because git cannot re-include anything
# beneath an excluded directory and the manuscript below has to be re-included.
/paper/*
# The manuscript source is not an artefact, so it is tracked. Its figures and tables are
# generated, but they are the paper's evidence and have to travel with the submission;
# paper/Arxiv/analysis.py regenerates every one of them from results/.
!/paper/Arxiv/
!/paper/Topology_Constrained_Reconciliation_for_Zero_Shot_Forecastingof_Occupancy_and_Flow/
# LaTeX build products, in whichever manuscript directory produces them.
*.aux
*.bbl
*.blg
*.log
*.out
*.synctex.gz
*.fdb_latexmk
*.fls
logs/
